{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ aging workforce employers retirement skills)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_1154622543#9_2077761899","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1974","rank":1,"snippet":"Will there be a Baby Boomer brain drain? What impact will Boomers who remain in the workforce have? How will Boomers affect the career prospects of younger workers? Navigating a multi-generational workplace: Is your business prepared for Boomers who don’t plan to retire? Companies must be welcoming to an <cover>aging workforce: Employers must adjust to a new workforce dynamic: \" , \"segment\": \"A poll by AARP revealed that 48% of companies have not, and will not, do any strategic planning to analyze the impact on their businesses of retirement by their Boomer employees. There are many industries and occupations that will be severely impacted by Boomer retirements. Your company needs to do some forecasting and planning, and get ready. The AARP and the Society for Human Resource Management teamed up to create a free tool to help companies identify their potential skills </cover>gaps when their workforce faces retirement. Not only does it assess critical functions, it also takes a critical look at the programs in place to retain workers. Companies must be welcoming to an aging workforce: Just as Boomers need to make changes in order to fit into organizations that may very well "}}
