{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1440310662#4_3246484430","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another passage from the dedicated NIOSH/CDC 'Productive Aging and Work' page, directly addressing age-friendly workplaces and practical issues for an aging workforce, including older drivers, crash prevention, falls, age-awareness training, and organizational preparation.","learned":"Authoritative NIOSH evidence identifies workplace aging issues such as age-friendly workplace design, older-driver safety, fall risks, age-awareness training, and preparing organizations for an aging workforce."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1978","reason":"The NIOSH productive-aging query is returning authoritative, dedicated evidence about older workers, safety, health, and age-friendly workplaces; continue for more grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1978"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1440314704#0_3246487112","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1978","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1440314704#0_3246487112\" , \"end_char\": 1230.000000 , \"headings\": \"PRODUCTIVE AGING AND WORK PRODUCTIVE AGING AND WORK A Life-Span Perspective References \" , \"segment\": \"A Life-Span Perspective | <cover>NIOSH | CDC PRODUCTIVE AGING AND WORK minus Related Pages A Life-Span Perspective Within the context of work, a life-span perspective holds that patterns of change and transition occur throughout the working life. As a result, the scope of productive aging includes all age groups of workers and is not limited to “older </cover>workers,” however that group may be defined. Other assumptions of a life-span perspective include: The aging process is multidirectional and involves both losses and gains. As workers age, some dimensions of functioning decline, while others improve. For example, physical stamina gradually decreases with age, but accumulated knowledge or “wisdom” tends to gradually increase. These different “trajectories of change” are important to understand in designing a workplace where all workers are able to perform at an optimal level. The aging process is characterized by plasticity. The term plasticity refers to the "}}
